  "description": "Scan from .NET on Linux through SANE, the scanner framework most Linux scanner drivers use. List scanners, read and set their options, scan a page or a whole document feeder, and get the pixels back. Calls libsane directly with no dependencies, and puts SANE's single-threaded, global-state design behind an async API. Needs the native SANE library (libsane1 or sane-backends) and your scanner's driver.",
